[h1]Version 1.0.0 — Initial Release[/h1]

[quote]ACE Environment Extended (AEE) is a physically accurate environment simulation for Arma 3, extending ACE3. This is the first Workshop release.[/quote]

[b]Added[/b]
[list]
[*]Physically accurate atmosphere: elevation lapse rates, diurnal temperature cycles, true air density, Koppen biome classification, orographic precipitation, WMO 3-hour pressure tendency
[*]Thermal and physiological models: wet-bulb globe temperature (ISO 7243 heat-stress categories), NWS heat index, JAG/TTI wind chill, altitude acclimatisation with time-of-useful-consciousness hypoxia, ISO 17166 UV index with ozone absorption, hypothermia and dehydration risk
[*]Optics: thermal crossover, mirage, solar glare, Cn²-based atmospheric seeing, physical smoke dispersal, Atlas rain extinction, dew and frost on optics, snow blindness — all unified under a single post-process arbiter (no flicker)
[*]Mobility: SAE J1349 engine derating, slip-curve traction, mud accretion, Nash-cascade river water level, NRMM cone-index route degradation, momentum-theory helicopter lift
[*]Environmental: Arrhenius Q10 CBRN persistence, Rothermel fire spread, avalanche risk, Stefan freeze/thaw, flash-flood prediction, surface wetness, scent dispersion
[*]Maritime: harmonic tidal prediction (M2/S2/K1/O1), WMO Beaufort sea state, Pierson-Moskowitz wave height, magnetic compass deviation
[*]Radio: Friis free-space path loss with atmospheric ducting, ITU-R P.531 ionospheric absorption
[*]Atmospheric events: lightning, sandstorms, dust devils, microbursts, ICAO eddy-dissipation-rate turbulence, airframe icing
[*]Real-world weather input: reads a weather.json written by tools/weather_fetch.py (Open-Meteo, no API key)
[/list]

[b]Integrations[/b]
[list]
[*]ACE3: weather state feeds the Kestrel; heat index and WBGT published; WBGT and dehydration drive ACE3 medical vitals
[*]KAT: dehydration and hypoxia state feed KAT's circulation model
[*]ACM: CBRN persistence drives ACM's contamination state
[*]ACRE2 / TFAR: radio propagation index scales transmission range
[/list]

[b]Testing[/b]
[list]
[*]183 unit tests mirroring the physics models, run by a single command
[*]Ten-phase dedicated-server integration test in Docker
[*]Five-host compat verification against the real mods in a live server
[/list]
